  "flightAltitudeHorizonBody": "At {altitude} the horizon sits about {dip}° lower than on the ground, so the sun takes longer to set and dawn comes sooner. That moves Maghrib and Isha about twenty minutes later, and Fajr about twenty minutes earlier, than the times for the ground beneath you — each row shows its own shift. Which horizon governs the prayer is a question for your marja, not one this app can settle.",
